WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.760
- In Kherson, Russian forces

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.040
that occupied the city left months ago

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.570
but they're still active just

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.180
on the other side of the river behind me.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.530
The fighting, blackouts

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.890
and food shortages have
pushed many people to leave

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.890
and for the ones who have
stayed, uncertainty remains

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.350
as the country prepares
for fighting to intensify

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.730
ahead of what Ukrainians expect

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.552
will be a major Russian
offensive in the spring.

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:28.135
(Tetiana speaking in foreign language)

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.590
- So one year after the war started,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.450
we came to Kherson to see what's next

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.100
along the front lines in Ukraine.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.070
Kherson, which was largely spared damage

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.090
during the occupation

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.100
has now become a combat zone.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.930
Ukrainian forces have taken up positions

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.730
inside the city where there's more cover

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.310
from incoming fire and
are launching artillery

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.050
at the Russians across the river.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.400
The Russians are shooting back

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.477
and the sound of shells
is now constant here.

00:00:52.477 --> 00:00:55.320
(booming sound)

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.143
Ukrainian forces deny
firing from within the city.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.580
(Dmytro speaking in foreign language)

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.460
- [Ian] We've heard the sound
of outgoing artillery fire

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.817
in central Kherson during
multiple reporting trips.

00:01:14.817 --> 00:01:15.870
(booming sound)

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.900
The fighting is unlikely
to stop anytime soon.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.420
Ukrainian forces have
remissions onto the far side

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.000
of the river, but
reclaiming the huge swath

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.760
of territory that Russians
still control on the far bank

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.813
is a tall order.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.470
Bosman is a Ukrainian soldier

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.515
in the trenches near the Dnieper river.

00:01:33.515 --> 00:01:38.098
(solider speaking in foreign language)

00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:50.190
- Though Kherson is not a strategic hub,

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.500
it is symbolically important for Moscow.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.740
It was the only regional capital
Russia captured last year.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.990
So it was central to any
claims the Kremlin made

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.250
that the war had been a success.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.780
But there was fierce resistance here

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.723
from the first days of the occupation.

00:02:02.723 --> 00:02:06.364
(crowd speaking in foreign language)

00:02:06.364 --> 00:02:09.281
(gunfire sounding)

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.170
- [Ian] Tetiana Kurilenko was one

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.648
of the Kherson residents
who took to the streets.

00:02:15.648 --> 00:02:20.231
(Tetiana speaking in foreign language)

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.180
- [Ian] Despite the protests,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.070
Moscow took steps to turn Kherson

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.183
into a Russian city.

00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:35.855
(Tetiana speaking in foreign language)

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.050
- Now a Ukrainian flag again flies

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.340
over the regional government building

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.810
in this square where thousands

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.607
of people greeted Ukrainian soldiers.

00:02:56.607 --> 00:03:00.030
(crowd cheering)

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.950
Many have fled since
those triumphant scenes.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.310
Today central Kherson is a
ghost town and bears scars

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.960
from Russian artillery fire
over the last few months.

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:10.470
(dramatic music)

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.110
At Tropinykh Hospital in central Kherson,

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.540
only a skeleton staff remains.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.000
But doctors say there's
enough medicine and workers

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.904
for the hospital to function.

00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:24.904
(Leonid speaking in foreign language)

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:27.150
- [Ian] Doctors are also
facing other challenges,

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.980
including treating patients with injuries

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.354
from Russian artillery.

00:03:30.354 --> 00:03:34.854
(Leonid speaking in foreign language)

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.310
- So after a year of war,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.950
residents of Kherson are
still unsure what lies ahead.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.930
Many have relatives on the
other side of the river

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.060
in occupied territory and have no idea

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.610
when they might see them again.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.830
On the ground, neither Russia nor Ukraine

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.300
has achieved a major breakthrough

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.567
since Kherson was liberated last year.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.200
(gun booming)

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.180
For now, fighting is concentrated

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.490
in Ukraine's east where a costly battle

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.380
of attrition could shape the war to come

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.390
with Russia using its manpower advantage

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.000
to slowly claw back territory.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.160
Ukraine is pushing
Western allies for weapons

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.743
that would help them retake
territory this spring.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.730
And any negotiations to
end the war still appear

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.903
to be a long way off.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.350
For the people who remain in Kherson,

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.080
they know that even if Ukraine
makes progress in the war,

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.708
rebuilding will take years.

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:35.375
(pensive music)

